//? Title: InfoVAE and MMD-VAE: Local KL and Aggregate Matching
//? Subtitle: Explicit Gaussian samples, signed unbiased IMQ discrepancy and separate validation objectives
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
InfoVAE combines pixel reconstruction, local posterior KL and a discrepancy between sampled
aggregate posterior codes and independent prior draws. This report runs matched alpha0.5
InfoVAE and alpha1 MMD-VAE teaching models with lambda10 on 294 known-factor binary images.
Both receive 21 explicit Adam updates and select epoch3 by their own fixed four-draw validation
objective. Test objectives are 404.911/403.818; the separate diagnostic negative ELBOs are
406.237/410.269 nats per image. Decode(mu) MSE0.15241/0.15471 is worse than the fitting mean
0.04855. Signed unbiased MMD, unfiltered images and poor generation remain visible. The
objectives differ across variants; neither their optimized values nor this tiny short run
establish mutual information, useful disentanglement or superiority on an image benchmark.
)
\toc

> A local posterior and an aggregate discrepancy

[Zhao, Song and Ermon's InfoVAE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.02262) separates local posterior
regularization from aggregate matching. In this small adaptation the encoder is
784→16 tanh→two four-coordinate linear Gaussian heads; the decoder is 4→16 tanh→784 logits.
Ten Glorot/zero-bias tensors contain 26,104 scalars. Explicit epsilon gives
z=mu+exp(l/2)⊙epsilon. The decoder uses only z; sigmoid logits give pixel probabilities,
not sampled binary pixels. A separate caller-supplied standard-normal sample y enters the
aggregate discrepancy, with no image-to-decoder or prior-sample-to-decoder bypass.

$$
\mathcal J_{\alpha,\lambda}=
\frac1B\sum_b\left[\operatorname{NLL}_b+(1-\alpha)\operatorname{KL}_b\right]
+(\alpha+\lambda-1)\widehat{\operatorname{MMD}}_u^2(z,y).
$$
\alttext(The objective averages summed pixel NLL and local Gaussian KL over images, then adds a weighted signed aggregate discrepancy between sampled codes and independent prior draws.)

Here alpha∈[0,1], lambda≥1. Pixel NLL sums 784 features, Gaussian KL sums four coordinates,
and only cases are averaged. MMD acts on sampled **z**, not posterior means. Prior independence
is the caller's statistical responsibility. Alpha1 removes local KL while retaining aggregate
regularization. Mean(NLL+KL) is reported separately as a negative-ELBO diagnostic; the general
training objective is not an ordinary ELBO or a direct mutual-information estimator.

