> A hand-checkable signed two-sample discrepancy

Use the equally averaged fixed inverse-multiquadric kernels
k(a,b)=(1/(1+d²)+4/(4+d²)+16/(16+d²))/3, with d²=||a−b||².
No dimension scaling, learned bandwidth or single-kernel substitution is used. For x with N
rows and y with M rows, N,M≥2 may differ:

$$
\widehat{\operatorname{MMD}}_u^2=
\frac{\sum_{i\ne j}k(x_i,x_j)}{N(N-1)}+
\frac{\sum_{i\ne j}k(y_i,y_j)}{M(M-1)}-
\frac{2\sum_{i,j}k(x_i,y_j)}{NM}.
$$
\alttext(Within-sample sums exclude self-pairs and have separate unequal-count denominators. Every cross pair remains, including corresponding indices when the counts match.)

The [unbiased quadratic estimator of Gretton et al.](https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v13/gretton12a.html)
can be negative at finite sample size. This is squared MMD, with no square root, zero clipping
or calibrated hypothesis-test p-value. With x=y=[0,1], let k01=(1/2+4/5+16/17)/3=127/170.
Each within mean is k01 and the full cross mean is (1+k01)/2, giving k01−1=−43/170.
Self-comparison is not an independent two-sample experiment. All-zero independent samples
instead give exactly zero. The next plot also evaluates unequal samples x=[0,1], y=[0,2,3].

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/info_mmd.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  namespace m  = n::models;
  const auto t = n::DType::Float64;
  auto       x = n::tensor({0., 1.}, {2, 1}, t), y = n::tensor({0., 2., 3.}, {3, 1}, t);
  auto       same = m::ImqMmd(x, x), different = m::ImqMmd(x, y);
  if (std::abs(same.value.item() + 43. / 170) > 1e-14)
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "| sample comparison | within x | within y | cross | signed MMD squared "
      "|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| same [0,1] | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n| unequal "
      "[0,1]/[0,2,3] | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      same.within_x.item(),
      same.within_y.item(),
      same.cross.item(),
      same.value.item(),
      different.within_x.item(),
      different.within_y.item(),
      different.cross.item(),
      different.value.item());
  std::vector<double> shift, value;
  for (int i = 0; i <= 40; ++i) {
    double d = i / 10.;
    shift.push_back(d);
    value.push_back(m::ImqMmd(x, x + d).value.item());
  }
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(shift, value, "signed unbiased MMD", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .title("Finite-sample MMD / two-point samples")
      .x_label("shift of second sample")
      .y_label("signed MMD squared")
      .save_svg("build/info_mmd.svg");
}
