> Objective coefficients by hand

For NLL=[4,6], KL=[2,4] and signed MMD=0.25, alpha0.5/lambda10 gives
5+0.5×3+9.5×0.25=8.875. Alpha1/lambda10 gives 5+10×0.25=7.5, with zero local KL.
Alpha0/lambda1 gives 5+3=8, the ordinary negative-ELBO expression. The alpha0.5 objective
partials are 1/2 for each NLL value, 1/4 for each KL value and 9.5 for MMD.

Float32 controls and coefficients retain the source's Float32 arithmetic; Float64 uses full
precision. The native objective preserves signed finite estimates. A full forward still
computes kernel diagnostics and requires both samples to have at least two rows even if the
aggregate coefficient is zero. There is no annealing, batch-statistics update or hidden fitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/info_coefficients.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto a = n::tensor({4., 6.}).requires_grad_(), b = n::tensor({2., 4.}).requires_grad_(),
       c    = n::scalar(.25).requires_grad_();
  auto loss = n::models::InfoVaeObjective(a, b, c);
  auto g    = n::grad(loss, {a, b, c});
  if (loss.item() != 8.875 || g[2].item() != 9.5)
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "InfoVAE8.875 / MMD-VAE{:.3f} / base negative ELBO{:.3f}; derivatives NLL{} KL{} MMD{}.\n",
      n::models::InfoVaeObjective(a, b, c, 1).item(),
      n::models::InfoVaeObjective(a, b, c, 0, 1).item(),
      g[0].values_str(),
      g[1].values_str(),
      g[2].item());
  std::vector<double> alpha, local, aggregate;
  for (int i = 0; i <= 20; ++i) {
    double v = i / 20.;
    alpha.push_back(v);
    local.push_back(1 - v);
    aggregate.push_back(v + 9);
  }
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(alpha, local, "local KL coefficient", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(alpha, aggregate, "aggregate MMD coefficient", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .title("InfoVAE coefficients / lambda10")
      .x_label("alpha")
      .y_label("coefficient")
      .save_svg("build/info_coefficients.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
InfoVAE8.875 / MMD-VAE7.500 / base negative ELBO8.000; derivatives NLL[0.5, 0.5] KL[0.25, 0.25] MMD9.5.
\image(figures/info_coefficients.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Alpha moves weight from the local KL term toward aggregate matching under fixed lambda10; changing the weights changes the selection objective too.)
\alttext(The local KL coefficient decreases from one to zero, while the aggregate MMD coefficient rises from nine to ten.)

> Native preparation and explicit paired training

The native offline beta-vae-assets preparation exhausts 294 unique binary 28×28 images:
2 shapes×3 sizes×7 x×7 y. Circles/squares have radius=size+2 and center=(3x+5,3y+5), with
inclusive Euclidean/Chebyshev radii. Residue(x+2y+size+3shape) mod7 assigns test0,
validation1, fit2–6, giving 210/42/42 disjoint combinations. This structured tiny teaching
lattice is not an IID benchmark, MNIST/dSprites or a semantic-information measurement.
Factors are not inputs, targets or checkpoint criteria; no factor probe is fitted here.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build/info_vae/info_vae");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
  auto                       arrays = n::load_npz((cache / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  std::set<int>              ids;
  std::set<std::vector<int>> images;
  for (auto& [name, value] : arrays) {
    if (name.ends_with("_images")) {
      for (int b = 0; b < value.size(0); ++b) {
        auto row = n::select(value, 0, b).to_vector<int>();
        if (!images.insert(row).second)
          return 1;
      }
      value = n::cast(value, n::DType::Float32);
    }
    if (name.ends_with("_source_ids"))
      for (int id : value.to_vector<int>())
        if (!ids.insert(id).second)
          return 1;
  }
  if (ids.size() != 294 || images.size() != 294)
    return 1;
  for (const std::string variant : {"info_vae", "mmd_vae"}) {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build/info_vae/" + variant);
    n::save_npz("build/info_vae/" + variant + "/data.npz", arrays);
  }
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "beta_vae/manifest.json",
      "build/info_vae/data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print(
      "| split | images | features |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| fit |210|784|\n| validation |42|784|\n| "
      "test |42|784|\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| split | images | features |
|---|---:|---:|
| fit |210|784|
| validation |42|784|
| test |42|784|
// result_end

Both variants use the same seed3901 parameter arrays, BatchOrder(210,32,3989), posterior banks
and independent prior banks. Each epoch has seven updates, including the final 18-image batch;
three epochs give 21 Adam steps per model at learning rate0.003, moments0.9/0.999, epsilon1e-8.
Epoch training posterior/prior seeds are 4002/4014,4003/4015,4004/4016. Fixed four-draw banks
use posterior fit3911/validation3917/test3923 and prior fit3943/validation3949/test3955.
Prior generation uses seed3967. All Float64 MT19937/Box–Muller banks and Float32 casts are saved.

Each completed epoch1–3 is eligible. The fixed four-draw validation **own objective** selects
its checkpoint; alpha0.5 and alpha1 optimize different criteria. They share data and draws,
not a common objective. Test values never select an epoch. NLL/KL accumulate per-row Float32
values in Float64, while scalar MMD/objective/negative-ELBO values retain the source reductions.
The full editable program exposes every gradient, Adam step, saved epoch and fresh restore.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <chrono>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <fstream>
namespace nn = dm::nn;
void Require(bool condition, const std::string& why) {
  if (!condition)
    throw std::runtime_error(why);
}
void Near(double x, double y, double tolerance, const std::string& why) {
  Require(std::abs(x - y) <= tolerance, why);
}
struct BetaFactorData {
  nn::Tensor images, factors, source;
};
struct VaeNoiseBank {
  nn::Tensor standard, epsilon;
};
nn::Tensor Flatten(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return nn::reshape(t, {t.size(0), 784});
}
nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& key) {
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
    if (k == key)
      return v;
  throw std::runtime_error(key);
}
std::vector<float> Bytes(const nn::Tensor& t) {
  return t.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
}
nn::NamedTensors Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  for (const auto& k : p.names())
    a.emplace_back(k, p.at(k).detach().clone());
  return a;
}
auto Snapshot(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  return p.flatten();
}
nn::NamedTensors CheckGradients(
    const nn::ParameterStore&      p,
    const std::vector<nn::Tensor>& gs,
    const std::string&,
    const std::string&) {
  nn::NamedTensors a;
  Require(gs.size() == p.size(), "all10 gradients");
  const auto names = p.names();
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gs.size(); ++i) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (double x : gs[i].to_vector<double>()) {
      Require(std::isfinite(x), "finite derivatives");
      norm += x * x;
    }
    Require(norm > 0, "nonzero derivative in each tensor");
    a.emplace_back(names[i], gs[i]);
  }
  return a;
}
VaeNoiseBank BetaVaeNoise(std::int64_t n, std::int64_t samples, std::uint32_t seed) {
  const auto standard = nn::models::GaussianNoise({n, 4}, samples, seed);
  return {standard, nn::cast(standard, nn::DType::Float32)};
}
nn::Tensor BetaVaeNoiseAt(const VaeNoiseBank& bank, int k) {
  return nn::select(bank.epsilon, 0, k).contiguous();
}

nn::NamedTensors Evaluate(
    nn::ParameterStore& p,
    const nn::Tensor&   images,
    const nn::Tensor&   noise,
    const nn::Tensor&   prior,
    double              alpha) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  auto o = nn::models::InfoVariationalAutoencoder(p, Flatten(images), noise, prior, alpha, 10);
  nn::NamedTensors out{
      {"mu", o.mu},
      {"log_variance", o.log_variance},
      {"z", o.z},
      {"logits", o.logits},
      {"probability", o.probability},
      {"nll", o.nll},
      {"kl", o.kl},
      {"negative_elbo", o.negative_elbo},
      {"mmd_xx", o.mmd_xx},
      {"mmd_yy", o.mmd_yy},
      {"mmd_xy", o.mmd_xy},
      {"mmd_within_x", o.mmd_within_x},
      {"mmd_within_y", o.mmd_within_y},
      {"mmd_cross", o.mmd_cross},
      {"mmd", o.mmd},
      {"loss", o.loss}};
  for (auto& [name, t] : out) {
    t = t.contiguous();
    for (float v : t.to_vector<float>())
      Require(std::isfinite(v), "all sixteen InfoVAE fields finite");
  }
  return out;
}
nn::Tensor Decode(nn::ParameterStore& p, const nn::Tensor& code) {
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  return nn::sigmoid(nn::models::InfoVaeDecode(p, code)).contiguous();
}
bool SameBytes(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return a.dtype() == b.dtype() && a.shape() == b.shape() && Bytes(a) == Bytes(b);
}
nn::Tensor PixelMean(const nn::Tensor& image) {
  auto               x = Flatten(image).to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<float> mean(784);
  for (int j = 0; j < 784; ++j) {
    double sum = 0;
    for (int b = 0; b < image.size(0); ++b)
      sum += x[b * 784 + j];
    mean[j] = float(sum / image.size(0));
  }
  return nn::from_vector(mean, {784});
}
nn::Tensor Constant(const nn::Tensor& row, int n) {
  return nn::broadcast_to(row.reshape({1, 784}), {n, 784}).contiguous();
}
double Mse(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  return nn::mean(
             nn::square(
                 nn::cast(Flatten(a), nn::DType::Float64) -
                 nn::cast(Flatten(b), nn::DType::Float64)))
      .item();
}
double Difference(const nn::Tensor& a, const nn::Tensor& b) {
  Require(a.shape() == b.shape(), "matching outputs");
  const auto x = a.contiguous().to_vector<float>(), y = b.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
  double     d = 0;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i)
    d = std::max(d, std::abs(double(x[i]) - y[i]));
  return d;
}
float Scalar(const nn::NamedTensors& f, const std::string& name) {
  return Find(f, name).item<float>();
}

/// {NLL, KL, MMD, objective, negative ELBO} averaged over 4 fixed posterior/prior draws.
std::vector<double> Score(
    nn::ParameterStore& model,
    const nn::Tensor&   x,
    const VaeNoiseBank& noise,
    const VaeNoiseBank& prior,
    double              alpha) {
  std::vector<double> sum(5);
  const auto          n = x.size(0);
  for (int k = 0; k < 4; ++k) {
    auto       f   = Evaluate(model, x, BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise, k), BetaVaeNoiseAt(prior, k), alpha);
    const auto nll = Find(f, "nll").to_vector<float>(), kl = Find(f, "kl").to_vector<float>();
    double     a = 0, b = 0;
    for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i)
      a += nll[i], b += kl[i];
    sum[0] += a / n;
    sum[1] += b / n;
    sum[2] += Scalar(f, "mmd");
    sum[3] += Scalar(f, "loss");
    sum[4] += Scalar(f, "negative_elbo");
  }
  for (auto& v : sum)
    v /= 4;
  return sum;
}

void Algebra(const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  auto nll = nn::tensor({4., 6.}).requires_grad_(), kl = nn::tensor({2., 4.}).requires_grad_(),
       mmd     = nn::scalar(.25).requires_grad_();
  auto info    = nn::models::InfoVaeObjective(nll, kl, mmd, .5f, 10.f),
       mmdonly = nn::models::InfoVaeObjective(nll, kl, mmd, 1.f, 10.f),
       vae     = nn::models::InfoVaeObjective(nll, kl, mmd, 0.f, 1.f);
  auto g       = nn::grad(info, {nll, kl, mmd});
  Near(info.item<float>(), 8.875, 0, "InfoVAE .5KL+9.5MMD");
  Near(mmdonly.item<float>(), 7.5, 0, "MMDVAE0KL+10MMD");
  Near(vae.item<float>(), 8, 0, "alpha0lambda1 EXACTbaseVAE");
  const auto gn = g[0].to_vector<float>(), gk = g[1].to_vector<float>();
  Require(
      gn == std::vector<float>{.5f, .5f} && gk == std::vector<float>{.25f, .25f} &&
          g[2].item<float>() == 9.5f,
      "InfoVAE coefficient partials");
  nn::NoGradGuard guard;
  nn::save_npz(
      (root / "coefficient_algebra.npz").string(),
      {{"info", info.detach()},
       {"mmd_only", mmdonly.detach()},
       {"vae", vae.detach()},
       {"gradient_nll", g[0]},
       {"gradient_kl", g[1]},
       {"gradient_mmd", g[2]}});
}

double Run(
    const std::vector<BetaFactorData>& pools,
    const std::filesystem::path&       root,
    int                                epochs,
    float                              alpha,
    const std::string&                 init) {
  std::filesystem::create_directories(root);
  std::vector<VaeNoiseBank> priors, noise;
  nn::NamedTensors          bank;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    noise.push_back(BetaVaeNoise(pools[k].images.size(0), 4, 3911 + k * 6));
    priors.push_back(BetaVaeNoise(pools[k].images.size(0), 4, 3943 + k * 6));
    bank.emplace_back(split + "_standard", noise[k].standard);
    bank.emplace_back(split + "_epsilon", noise[k].epsilon);
    bank.emplace_back(split + "_prior_standard", priors[k].standard);
    bank.emplace_back(split + "_prior_epsilon", priors[k].epsilon);
  }
  auto generation = BetaVaeNoise(20, 1, 3967);
  bank.emplace_back("generation_standard", generation.standard);
  bank.emplace_back("generation_epsilon", generation.epsilon);
  nn::save_npz((root / "fixed_noise.npz").string(), bank);
  nn::ParameterStore model(3901);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    nn::models::InfoVariationalAutoencoder(
        model, nn::zeros({2, 784}), nn::zeros({2, 4}), nn::zeros({2, 4}), alpha, 10);
  }
  nn::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  nn::Optimizer optimizer(model, .003, config);
  if (!init.empty())
    model.load(init);
  Require(model.count() == 26104 && model.size() == 10, "small InfoVAE census");
  nn::save_npz((root / "initial_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(model));
  nn::BatchOrder order(210, 32, 3989);
  std::ofstream  history(root / "history.tsv"), batches(root / "batches.tsv");
  history.precision(17);
  history << "epoch\tvalidation_nll\tvalidation_kl\tvalidation_mmd\tvalidation_"
             "objective\tvalidation_negative_elbo\n";
  batches << "epoch\tstep\trow\tsource_id\n";
  const auto fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<int>();
  const auto best_path  = (root / "best.npz").string();
  double     best       = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int        selected = 0, steps = 0;
  const auto started = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= epochs; ++epoch) {
    auto e = BetaVaeNoise(210, 1, 4001 + epoch), p = BetaVaeNoise(210, 1, 4013 + epoch);
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("train_noise_epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz")).string(),
        {{"standard", e.standard},
         {"epsilon", e.epsilon},
         {"prior_standard", p.standard},
         {"prior_epsilon", p.epsilon}});
    auto epsilon = BetaVaeNoiseAt(e, 0), prior = BetaVaeNoiseAt(p, 0);
    order.begin_epoch();
    int seen = 0;
    for (;;) {
      auto rows = order.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      auto x = nn::take_rows(pools[0].images, rows), ep = nn::take_rows(epsilon, rows),
           pr = nn::take_rows(prior, rows);
      if (steps == 0) {
        nn::save_npz(
            (root / "first_batch.npz").string(), {{"images", x}, {"epsilon", ep}, {"prior", pr}});
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_forward.npz").string(), Evaluate(model, x, ep, pr, alpha));
        nn::save_npz(
            (root / "first_gradients.npz").string(),
            CheckGradients(
                model,
                nn::grad(
                    nn::models::InfoVariationalAutoencoder(model, Flatten(x), ep, pr, alpha, 10)
                        .loss,
                    model.parameters()),
                "all InfoVAE derivatives finite",
                "all10tensors receive InfoVAE gradients"));
      }
      auto train = nn::models::InfoVariationalAutoencoder(model, Flatten(x), ep, pr, alpha, 10);
      optimizer.step(nn::grad(train.loss, model.parameters()));
      if (steps == 0)
        nn::save_npz((root / "first_update_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(model));
      for (auto row : rows)
        batches << epoch << '\t' << steps << '\t' << row << '\t' << fit_source[row] << '\n';
      ++steps;
      seen += int(rows.size());
    }
    Require(seen == 210, "all fit cases once per epoch");
    auto score = Score(model, pools[1].images, noise[1], priors[1], alpha);
    history << epoch;
    for (auto v : score)
      history << '\t' << v;
    history << '\n';
    nn::save_npz(
        (root / ("epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "_arrays.npz")).string(), Arrays(model));
    if (score[3] < best) {
      best     = score[3];
      selected = epoch;
      model.save(best_path); // fixed 4-draw validation InfoVAE objective selects checkpoint
    }
  }
  const double seconds =
      std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - started).count();
  nn::ParameterStore deployed(3901);
  {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    nn::models::InfoVariationalAutoencoder(
        deployed, nn::zeros({2, 784}), nn::zeros({2, 4}), nn::zeros({2, 4}), alpha, 10);
  }
  deployed.load(best_path); // fresh InfoVAE model-only restore
  Near(
      Score(deployed, pools[1].images, noise[1], priors[1], alpha)[3],
      best,
      1e-8,
      "restored fixednoise validation objective");
  const auto       before = Snapshot(deployed);
  nn::NamedTensors outputs;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    auto              mean  = Evaluate(
        deployed,
        pools[k].images,
        nn::zeros({pools[k].images.size(0), 4}),
        BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[k], 0),
        alpha);
    Require(Bytes(Find(mean, "z")) == Bytes(Find(mean, "mu")), "epsilon0 gives mu");
    for (const auto& [key, v] : mean)
      outputs.emplace_back(split + "_zero_" + key, v);
    for (int draw = 0; draw < 4; ++draw) {
      auto f = Evaluate(
          deployed,
          pools[k].images,
          BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[k], draw),
          BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[k], draw),
          alpha);
      for (const auto& [key, v] : f)
        outputs.emplace_back(split + "_draw" + std::to_string(draw) + "_" + key, v);
    }
  }
  auto ep = BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 0), pr = BetaVaeNoiseAt(priors[2], 0);
  auto test   = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, ep, pr, alpha),
       repeat = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, ep, pr, alpha),
       other  = Evaluate(deployed, pools[2].images, BetaVaeNoiseAt(noise[2], 1), pr, alpha);
  const auto probability = Find(test, "probability");
  Require(
      SameBytes(probability, Find(repeat, "probability")) &&
          SameBytes(probability, Decode(deployed, Find(test, "z"))),
      "repeat/code-only decoder BITEXACT");
  Require(
      SameBytes(Find(test, "mu"), Find(other, "mu")) &&
          !SameBytes(Find(test, "z"), Find(other, "z")) &&
          !SameBytes(probability, Find(other, "probability")),
      "Gaussiannoise affects z/decoder,not posteriorheads");
  auto small = Evaluate(
      deployed,
      nn::take_rows(pools[2].images, {0, 1}),
      nn::take_rows(ep, {0, 1}),
      nn::take_rows(pr, {0, 1, 2}),
      alpha);
  const double parity = Difference(Find(small, "probability"), nn::take_rows(probability, {0, 1}));
  Require(parity < 2e-6, "posterior reconstruction smallbatch/unequalprior parity");
  auto prior_z = BetaVaeNoiseAt(generation, 0), prior = Decode(deployed, prior_z);
  nn::save_npz((root / "prior.npz").string(), {{"z", prior_z}, {"probability", prior}});
  nn::save_npz((root / "outputs.npz").string(), outputs);
  nn::save_npz((root / "model_arrays.npz").string(), Arrays(deployed));
  Require(before == Snapshot(deployed), "InfoVAE all inference immutable");
  auto          score            = Score(deployed, pools[2].images, noise[2], priors[2], alpha);
  auto          mean             = Constant(PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42);
  const auto    zero_probability = Find(outputs, "test_zero_probability");
  const double  mse = Mse(zero_probability, pools[2].images), baseline = Mse(mean, pools[2].images);
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta.precision(17);
  meta << "{\"parameters\":26104,\"tensors\":10,\"epochs\":" << epochs << ",\"updates\":" << steps
       << ",\"alpha\":" << alpha << ",\"lambda\":10,\"local_kl_weight\":" << 1 - alpha
       << ",\"aggregate_mmd_weight\":" << alpha + 9 << ",\"selected_epoch\":" << selected
       << ",\"mc_samples\":4,\"test_nll\":" << score[0] << ",\"test_kl\":" << score[1]
       << ",\"test_mmd\":" << score[2] << ",\"test_objective\":" << score[3]
       << ",\"test_diagnostic_negative_elbo\":" << score[4] << ",\"decode_mu_mse\":" << mse
       << ",\"fit_mean_mse\":" << baseline << ",\"small_batch_max_error\":" << parity
       << ",\"training_seconds\":" << seconds << "}\n";
  Require(bool(meta) && bool(history) && bool(batches), "complete InfoVAE evidence");
  std::print(
      "| {:.1f} | {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",
      alpha,
      selected,
      score[0],
      score[1],
      score[2],
      score[3],
      score[4],
      mse);
  return seconds;
}

int main() {
  auto                        data = nn::load_npz("build/info_vae/info_vae/data.npz");
  std::vector<BetaFactorData> pools;
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"})
    pools.push_back(
        {Find(data, split + "_images"),
         Find(data, split + "_factors"),
         Find(data, split + "_source_ids")});
  Algebra("build/info_vae");
  std::print(
      "| alpha | selected epoch | test NLL | test KL | test signed MMD | own objective | "
      "diagnostic negative ELBO | decode(mu) MSE |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  Run(pools, "build/info_vae/info_vae", 3, .5f, "");
  Run(pools, "build/info_vae/mmd_vae", 3, 1.f, "");
  auto a = nn::load_npz("build/info_vae/info_vae/initial_arrays.npz"),
       b = nn::load_npz("build/info_vae/mmd_vae/initial_arrays.npz");
  for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
    Require(SameBytes(value, Find(b, key)), "both variants have exact matched initialization");
  std::print(
      "Fitting-mean test MSE {:.12f}; both variants retain all 21 updates and own validation "
      "selection.\n",
      Mse(Constant(PixelMean(pools[0].images), 42), pools[2].images));
}
```
