> Unfiltered reconstructions and image-free prior probabilities

For each model, ten evenly spaced test indices floor(k×41/9) are shown without filtering:
original, decode(mu), one posterior-draw probability image, fitting-only mean. The common
grayscale is[0,1]. Decode(mu) is not the posterior predictive mean. The final prior gallery
uses the same twenty standard-normal codes through the selected tanh decoders, with no image,
encoder or MMD evaluation. These are probabilities, not Bernoulli pixel draws.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/info_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto find   = [](const n::NamedTensors& a, const std::string& key) {
    for (auto& [k, t] : a)
      if (k == key)
        return t;
    throw std::runtime_error(key);
  };
  std::vector<n::Tensor>    panels;
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i)
    rows.push_back(i * 41 / 9);
  for (const std::string model : {"info_vae", "mmd_vae"}) {
    auto data = n::load_npz("build/info_vae/" + model + "/data.npz"),
         out  = n::load_npz("build/info_vae/" + model + "/outputs.npz");
    auto mean = n::mean(find(data, "fit_images").reshape({210, 784}), {0}, true);
    for (const auto& t : std::vector<n::Tensor>{
             find(data, "test_images"),
             find(out, "test_zero_probability"),
             find(out, "test_draw0_probability"),
             n::broadcast_to(mean, {42, 784})})
      panels.push_back(n::take_rows(t, rows).reshape({10, 28, 28, 1}));
  }
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::concat(panels, 0), "build/info_reconstructions.png", 10, 0, 1, 4, 220. / 255, 3);
}
