> Reproduction evidence and binding scope

All35 original source archives are compared by dtype, shape and every value byte, including
coefficient algebra, data/noise, initial/first-update/every-epoch/selected weights, first
gradients, all sixteen fields for the zero/four-draw evaluations of every pool and prior
codes/probabilities. Both complete histories and batch/source orders match exactly. The optional
independent NumPy oracle checks all first parameter derivatives, both exact first Adam steps,
every saved kernel/within/cross term, Gaussian banks and all six eligible validation criteria.
It does not fit models or prepare/download data.

```
python3 scripts/check_info_variational_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/info_vae --json build/nn-report-conversion/info_vae/oracle.json
```

Native functions are ImqKernel, ImqMmd, InfoVaeObjective, InfoVaeDecode and
InfoVariationalAutoencoder, exposed in Python and R. All seven MMD and sixteen full-model
fields own lifetime. Tests cover live Float64 image/noise/prior gradients, caller-owned Adam,
unequal counts, signed estimates and image-free decoding through collection. This reusable
API/report conversion does not mark independent Python/R experiment loops as completed ports.
The shared WAE kernel adapter delegates to canonical C++ after separate original-run parity;
its required compatibility include remains until that example is converted. GAN diagnostics'
independent value-only copy remains for their later conversions.
